.yarn/

# --- Local user state ---
# .vscode: as configuracoes COMPARTILHADAS (tasks, launch, settings,
# extensions) sao versionadas de proposito - fazem parte do setup de dev.
# Qualquer outro arquivo local do editor continua fora.
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/tasks.json
!.vscode/launch.json
.idea/
.claude/
*.iml
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# --- Aurora runtime artefacts ---
components/Projeto/
components/Temp/
components/Backup/
*.spf.bak
*.aurora_backup

# --- Bundled toolchain binaries ---
# These ship via GitHub Releases (see RELEASE.md). They are NOT tracked
# in git history. The bootstrap step downloads them into components/Packages/
# on first launch. If you bring your own toolchain locally, drop it in the
# matching directory and it will Just Work.
components/Packages/
saphoComponents/Packages/

# Bibliotecas Python instaladas pelo painel, mais o manifesto e o cache do
# catalogo remoto. Tudo estado POR MAQUINA: o que se versiona e a LISTA
# (resources/pylib-catalog.json), nunca o que foi instalado nesta copia.
components/PyLibs/

# Manual do SAPHO. E gerado e publicado pelo repositorio nipscernlab/docs_aurora;
# download-docs.js traz o pacote da Release a cada bootstrap, como a toolchain.
# Versionar aqui duplicaria alguns megabytes de HTML, imagens e PDF, e a copia
# envelheceria em silencio a cada correcao de texto feita la.
resources/docs/

# Version manifest kept by scripts/verify-components.mts — per-machine record of
# which toolchain tag is installed for each component, used to detect a version
# bump on `npm install` / `npm run components:verify`. Never commit it.
components/.aurora-versions.json

# YANC compilers (cmmcomp, asmcomp, appcomp, comp2gtkw) — built from
# the separate nipscernlab/yanc repo. download-yanc.js fetches them
# from that repo's GitHub Releases at prestart, same model as the main
# toolchain bundle above.
components/bin/

# The SAPHO processor Verilog (core.v, ula.v, processor.v, instr_dec.v, ...),
# the C++ shim Headers (cmath, vector, ...) and the float-math Macros
# (float_sin.asm, ...). All three ship INSIDE the yanc release
# (yanc-bin-vX.zip carries bin/ + SAPHO/ + Header/ + Macros/) so they stay
# version-matched with the compilers that emit code against them.
# download-yanc.js extracts them, and the yanc's Scripts/aurora.bat (testing a
# local yanc) copies the same folders; do NOT commit a copy that can drift stale
# or show up as a spurious diff after every yanc bump (e.g. v5.1 swapped the LUT
# macros for minimax — committed copies would dirty every dev's working tree on
# the next `npm start`).
components/SAPHO/
components/Header/
components/Macros/
# Desde a v5.6 o zip do yanc traz tambem, na raiz, um README.md (o que e cada
# pasta) e example/ (um programa em C++ e em C+-); o download extrai o zip
# inteiro em components/, entao os dois caem la e vem do yanc, como as pastas.
components/README.md
components/example/

# --- Test scratch ---
coverage/
.nyc_output/

